# Cloudflare Pages response headers for app.zellavoice.com and admin.zellavoice.com (security audit 18 Nov 2026, M14).
# The Content Security Policy is REPORT ONLY for the site: browsers log what it would block, nothing is blocked.
# ENFORCING on the pages that hold Stripe's card fields (owner decision, 27 Nov 2026: card fields in our pages are
# approved on the condition that an enforcing CSP on them is a go live gate): the onboarding Pay step (/welcome/setup)
# and the CRM's payment pages (/app/settings/billing/pay/<invoice>, /app/settings/billing/pack/<code>), which the CRM
# opens as a full page load so this header applies. Same policy, enforced; the rest of the site stays report only.
# Sources, from the built app (web/dist): scripts and styles from this site; Google Fonts (index.html, and the font
# stylesheet the app reads, connect-src); Supabase for the
# API, realtime, edge functions and stored files. Vapi is allowed ahead of use. Stripe (owner, 27 Nov 2026): the payment
# pages load Stripe.js and mount Stripe's card fields and billing address (Elements) in Stripe's frames, so, as Stripe's
# integration security guide lists for Stripe.js and Checkout: script-src js.stripe.com and *.js.stripe.com; frame-src
# js.stripe.com, *.js.stripe.com, hooks.stripe.com (3D Secure) and checkout.stripe.com; connect-src api.stripe.com and
# checkout.stripe.com. Nothing else of Stripe's is needed by our page (the fields' own images and scripts load inside
# Stripe's frames, under Stripe's policy). Inline styles: React sets style attributes, so style-src needs
# 'unsafe-inline'. No inline scripts.
